{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mr5xad0sam6","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"ls20 run 20 bump probes need frontier plateau which 80 action budget never reaches","summary":"Run 20 live ls20: bump probes + cross run coverage persistence landed and pass full suite, but the live run fired 0 bumps. Root cause: bump discovery (and interaction discovery) only engage AFTER the movement frontier is declared exhausted, i.e. real coverage plateaus for coverage_plateau_exhaust=2 consecutive frontier batches. On the live 80-action budget the sweep grows slowly (frontier_batches=11, coverage_pct=0.05) and never plateaus for 2 in a row, so the exhaustion gate never trips and bumps never fire. The mechanism itself is correct: the push-block toy is solved end-to-end by a contact bump in tests, and _movement_direction_map must sample multiple reachable states (a single boxed-in cell hides directions like RIGHT). KB degraded gracefully: coverage-state search timed out (daemon slow) -> fresh sweep coverage_resumed_pct=0.0; coverage note write got HTTP 404 on /overlay/note -> coverage_persisted=false; ORIENT still adopted the warm-start program whole via native /note/get. To actually exercise bumps live, a future run should lower coverage_plateau_exhaust or raise the action budget so the movement frontier plateaus before budget exhaustion.","category":null,"tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-07-04T05:29:34.828Z","vec":[-0.04682578518986702,-0.0071084219962358475,0.015220971778035164,0.07431051135063171,0.06488078832626343,-0.0452871099114418,-0.04361754655838013,-0.0013848647940903902,-0.10102715343236923,0.02834869548678398,0.014426372945308685,0.029444213956594467,0.06580765545368195,-0.05093421787023544,0.04918366298079491,0.04135478287935257,-0.007493097800761461,-0.07517028599977493,-0.02586306631565094,-0.01962759718298912,0.0042963954620063305,0.015997299924492836,0.031633179634809494,0.038966014981269836,-0.06971604377031326,-0.043222133070230484,